Comparison operators bind to their operands: an over-long condition made
of one comparison between two atomic operands has no legal break point
and stays over-long rather than breaking before `>=` or `==`
(fmt.max_line_length "Wrapping never happens ... before comparison
operators").
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Compare;
:PARAMETERS oSettings;
:IF oSettings:primaryConfiguration:maximumAllowedRetryCount >= oSettings:fallbackConfiguration:limit;
:RETURN .T.;
:ENDIF;
:RETURN .F.;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Compare;
	:PARAMETERS oSettings;
	:IF oSettings:primaryConfiguration:maximumAllowedRetryCount >= oSettings:fallbackConfiguration:limit;
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN .F.;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
